Skip a relay token whose id attribute is negative.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why: parseIndexedTokens bounds the wire-supplied id only from above, so `id="-1"`
indexes the token slice at -1 and panics. onOffer calls it while holding e.mu, and
whatsmeow's handler recovery leaves that mutex locked, so every later call operation
on the client hangs. Measured with a probe: the unpatched parser panics with
`index out of range [-1]`. Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387,
round 10.

diff --git a/engine.go b/engine.go
index 2b88830..ee8517a 100644
--- a/engine.go
+++ b/engine.go
@@ -1769,7 +1769,9 @@ func parseIndexedTokens(node *waBinary.Node, tag string) [][]byte {
 				id = n
 			}
 		}
-		if id >= maxRelayTokens {
+		// The id is wire input: a negative one passed the upper bound and
+		// indexed the slice, panicking while onOffer holds e.mu.
+		if id < 0 || id >= maxRelayTokens {
 			continue
 		}
 		for len(tokens) <= id {
